; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Which Shapes Tile the Floor?
; CATEGORY: Geometry & Trigonometry
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     tessellation, regular polygons, interior angle, 360
; SUMMARY:  Fits copies of triangles, squares, pentagons and hexagons around one point to show why only three regular shapes can tile a floor.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Four panels each take one regular shape and put copies of it
;   corner to corner around a single point. Triangles, squares and
;   hexagons close up perfectly. Pentagons leave a gap, so they can
;   never cover a floor without holes.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. To try another shape, type for example
;     around.point 8 0 0 50
;   after a CLEARSCREEN.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the corner (interior angle) of a regular n-gon is 180 - 360/n
;   * shapes tile around a point only if their corners add to 360
;   * INT tells how many fit, and subtracting tells what is left over
;   * drawing the same shape again after a turn
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Try 8 sides. How big is the gap? (Bathroom floors fill it with
;     little squares.)
;   * Try 12 sides with triangles in the gaps.
;   * Use only two colors. Which panel then has two neighbors alike?
; ============================================================

to corner.angle :n
  output 180 - 360 / :n
end

; Put as many n-gons as will fit around the point x y.
to around.point :n :x :y :side
  localmake "corner corner.angle :n
  localmake "fits int (360 + 0.001) / :corner
  localmake "gap 360 - :fits * :corner
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 90
  setpensize 2 setpencolor [40 40 40]
  for [k 1 :fits] [
    ; cycle through three colors so neighbors stand out
    filled item 1 + remainder :k 3 [[255 190 90] [120 180 240] [150 220 140]] [
      pendown
      repeat :n [forward :side left 360 / :n]
    ]
    penup
    ; the next shape starts where this one's corner ends
    left :corner
  ]
  ; a red dot marks the shared point
  setpensize 10 setpencolor "red dot list :x :y
  ; the sum written underneath
  setpencolor "black
  penup setxy :x - 110 :y - 125
  label (sentence :fits "x round :corner "= round :fits * :corner)
  setxy :x - 110 :y - 147
  ifelse :gap < 0.01 [
    setpencolor "forest label [fits exactly: it tiles!]
  ] [
    setpencolor "red label (sentence [gap of] round :gap [degrees: no tiling])
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground "white
setlabelheight 16
around.point 3 -200 140 80
around.point 4 200 140 70
around.point 6 -200 -130 50
around.point 5 200 -130 55
